From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:07:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: send like stock mt76: no VO aggregation,
 PS hold or VoW setup

Where our fork sent more than stock OpenWrt's mt76 on normal traffic, go
back to stock by default, each behind a module parameter:

- vo_aggr (mt76-connac-lib, default off): no BA sessions on TIDs 6/7,
  as before upstream f67ffb60.
- ps_sync (default off): firmware PS sync events no longer hold a
  dozing station's frames; the hardware buffers them, as stock does (with the
  2026 firmware's event layout this was inert anyway).
- vow_stock (default on): no VoW setup at all (feature control, DRR
  quanta, deficit bound, per-station weights, VoW band); the firmware
  keeps its boot defaults and stations get stock's BSS group. vow_atf
  writes then fail with -EOPNOTSUPP.

Two more switches, off, for alternative settings: vow_fw_quanta (ATF without
WATF, the firmware's quantum table, station levels one down) and
muru_ofdma_ul (UL OFDMA in STA_REC_MURU).

KUnit: all mt76 suites pass (45).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
